+# DOT’s FY 2006 accountability report and the House transmittal
+
+Public derivative of the November 9, 2026 Eastern source review · B129 / PD03–PD05, with PD01–PD02 still open. This review follows the National Archives file-unit lead for the FY 2006 Performance and Accountability Report (PAR). The House recorded a transmittal of that annual report as **executive communication 10204**. Two separately released OIG reports and their attached management replies show what report-specific follow-up looked like in that publication. They identify comparison records and office routes for the FAA inquiry. The acquired items concern the annual report and its components. The corrected May 2003 answer, proof of receipt and the case-specific decision remain unacquired. [Prior catalog review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/87cd2d5d3a169830f87412d859a3f7da2992b901/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-rg398-public-catalog-crosswalk-2026-11-09/README.md)
+
+## Dates and recipients preserved by source
+
+| Source and locator | Exact field or value | Scope |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| NARA NAID 608696696, RG 398 export object `rg_398-269.jsonl` line 1 | `11/22/2006 Performance & Accountability Report FY 2006` | File-unit title in the Cino appointment series. The description has zero linked digital objects in the checked snapshot. [Catalog description](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/608696696) |
+| DOT public PAR, reader p. 8 of 412, printed p. 6, line 148 in this capture. Later House hearing, physical p. 113, printed p. 99, footnote 1 | `November 15, 2006` | Date printed under the Secretary’s message. The later prepared statement separately cites the PAR with the same date in a highway-safety discussion. [PAR message](https://www.transportation.gov/sites/dot.gov/files/docs/dot_annual_performance_report_fy_2006.pdf#page=8) · [Hearing footnote](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CHRG-110hhrg36688/pdf/CHRG-110hhrg36688.pdf#page=113) |
+| December 5, 2006 Congressional Record, physical p. 60, printed H8734, lines 1–3 and 120–124 | `December 5, 2006` · `10204.` · `Committee on Government Reform` | The House recorded a letter from the Secretary transmitting DOT’s FY 2006 PAR. The entry supplies a recipient and retrieval number. The signed cover, enclosure and committee intake are separate records. [House item 10204](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2006-12-05/pdf/CREC-2006-12-05.pdf#page=60) |
+
+These are a folder-title date, a dated message and citation, and a Congressional Record date. Preserve all three and their source fields. The accession folder and 10204 enclosure would be needed to establish their actual content and version relationship. The same House page also lists 10188, a Corporation for National and Community Service final-action report. The separately documented DOT House item 3550 concerns a Secretary’s management report for the period ending March 31, 2007. Keep those retrieval keys and report categories separate. [House item 10188, p. H8734](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2006-12-05/pdf/CREC-2006-12-05.pdf#page=60) · [Prior House 3550 review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/81c2a05871cd8cd689ee7f99c96b697acdd11837/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-house-recipient-oversight-records-2026-11-09/README.md)
+
+## Two report-specific response examples
+
+- **PT-2007-004**. The November 15 Scovel memorandum says `INFORMATION`, `J-1`, and addresses the Secretary and Deputy Secretary. It identifies ten **FY 2007** management challenges and says the report and DOT’s reply will be included in the **FY 2006** PAR. The OIG publication page says the report was included. The public PAR reader shows the same report number, date, routing and recipients. The OIG PDF’s appendix contains an October 31, 2006 `ACTION` memorandum from the Assistant Secretary for Budget and Programs/CFO to the Inspector General with comments on that draft. The appendix says additional technical comments had been supplied separately. This supplies an actual report-to-response pair and identifies a separate draft-comment record. [OIG memorandum, physical p. 2, lines 12–35](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/Final_OIG_Top_Mngt_Challenges.pdf#page=2) · [OST response, physical p. 60, printed p. 59, lines 10–45](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/Final_OIG_Top_Mngt_Challenges.pdf#page=60) · [OIG publication page, HTML lines 637 and 665](https://www.oig.dot.gov/library-item/30043) · [PAR copy, reader p. 335, lines 10969–10983](https://www.transportation.gov/sites/dot.gov/files/docs/dot_annual_performance_report_fy_2006.pdf#page=335)
+- **FI-2007-010**. The November 15 Scovel memorandum says `ACTION`, `JA–20`, and addresses the Secretary. It concerns the audit of consolidated financial statements and describes an FAA construction-in-progress accounting issue. The standalone appendix has a scanned November 14, 2006 reply from the Assistant Secretary for Budget and Programs/CFO to Scovel. The report records a promised detailed action plan by December 29, 2006. The appendix is the response and promise, and the actual later plan was outside this acquisition. Exhibit C lists QC-2007-009 and PT-2007-004 separately. The PAR reader shows the financial memorandum with the same date, routing and recipient. [Financial memorandum, physical p. 1, lines 10–41](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/CFO-rpt.pdf#page=1) · [OIG deadline summary, physical p. 21, lines 12–16](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/CFO-rpt.pdf#page=21) · [Management response, physical p. 27, attachment p. 23](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/CFO-rpt.pdf#page=27) · [Exhibit C, physical p. 26, lines 47–63](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/CFO-rpt.pdf#page=26) · [PAR copy, reader p. 255, lines 8264–8276](https://www.transportation.gov/sites/dot.gov/files/docs/dot_annual_performance_report_fy_2006.pdf#page=255)
+
+The held August 31 **CC-2006-085** cover is itself labeled `ACTION`, from Acting Inspector General Todd J. Zinser to the Acting Secretary and FAA Administrator. These three items show that the cover label occurs on records with different IDs, subjects, signers and recipients. PD03–PD04 still require a join keyed to CC-2006-085 or investigation 042R0122001. The financial action-plan date belongs to FI-2007-010. The annual management-challenge response belongs to PT-2007-004. [FAA investigation cover, physical p. 1, and recommendations, p. 12](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf#page=1)
+
+## Next records and limits
+
+- **House 10204 and NAID 608696696.** Seek the signed cover, actual enclosure/version list and committee intake for item 10204. For the Cino file unit, seek the November 22 briefing, any annotated agenda and enclosure list. Compare received versions, document dates and control numbers. Keep the separate October 20 FAA MAC Meeting catalog title and the absence of linked digital objects as recorded. Exact-date public searches yielded no minutes joined to that file unit. [October 20 catalog description](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/608696679)
+- **PD03–PD04 candidate record categories.** The PAR describes annual statements of assurance and associated remediation plans going to the Assistant Secretary for Budget and Programs/CFO. It separately names organizational accountability contracts and year-end organizational performance assessments, which can include work on OIG management challenges or weaknesses. These are specific records to check for a case identifier. Coverage of this investigation and any relation to personnel consideration remain untested. [PAR reader p. 33, printed p. 31, lines 775–781](https://www.transportation.gov/sites/dot.gov/files/docs/dot_annual_performance_report_fy_2006.pdf#page=33) · [PAR reader p. 88, printed p. 86, lines 2586–2600](https://www.transportation.gov/sites/dot.gov/files/docs/dot_annual_performance_report_fy_2006.pdf#page=88)
+- **PD01–PD03 retain priority.** The actual corrected May 2003 answer and recipient acknowledgment, a signed consideration/action/no-action decision, and the response and disposition records for each recommendation remain TODOs. The public cover and closing of the investigation, implementation, delivery and personnel action describe different events. Keep the p. 12 recommendations distinct from those continuing on p. 13. [FAA investigation report, physical pp. 12–13](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf#page=12)
+
+Five new HTTP 200 source bodies and three held bodies matched their recorded SHA-256 hashes. The four new PDF text layers, spanning 503 physical pages, and three selected image-backed page OCRs had zero matches to the bounded case-key and QFR phrase screen. That scope leaves unscanned page images, variant terms, unindexed file contents and the full PAR body outside the negative screen. The PAR is cited from selected official indexed passages. The earlier direct request returned HTTP 403 with zero bytes, so there is no PAR PDF-body hash in this unit. Page-face checks corroborate the House referral, the October 31 response heading, the November 14 reply date and the hearing footnote. The public derivative contains the analysis, source pins and text diff. [Source and verification ledger](SOURCE-PINS.json)
